exercises.solution:
Capacity is charge per gram, converted to mAh; the pair's capacity is a harmonic combination because both electrodes must hold the same charge:

```python
F = 96485.0

def capacity(n, molar_mass):
    return n * F / (3.6 * molar_mass)

def pair_energy(q_pos, q_neg, volts):
    return volts / (1 / q_pos + 1 / q_neg)
```

The harmonic form shows why improving the *weaker* electrode matters most. LiFePO₄ (170 mAh/g) with graphite (372) gives 385 Wh/kg of active material; replacing graphite by silicon (about 3580) would raise it only to about 540 Wh/kg, because the cathode then dominates the mass. Cathodes, not anodes, are the main bottleneck of lithium-ion energy.

